  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe current SLSQP-based approach gets stuck in local optima due to the non-convex nature of the problem. We propose using Particle Swarm Optimization (PSO) - a global optimization heuristic that maintains a swarm of candidate solutions and iteratively explores the solution space. PSO is particularly effective for non-convex problems and can escape local optima by maintaining velocity momentum and using social information from the swarm.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nWe represent h as a vector of n_points values in [0,1] with sum(h) = n_points/2. The objective is to minimize:\nC5 = max_k (h * (1 - h shifted by k))_sum * dx\nwith constraints: 0 <= h[i] <= 1 for all i, sum(h) = n_points / 2.\n\n3. Implementation procedure\na) Initialize swarm with m particles, each representing a candidate h vector.\nb) For each particle:\n   i) Compute overlap integral for all possible shifts k\n   ii) Evaluate current C5 value\nc) Update particle velocities based on:\n   i) Personal best (pbest)\n   ii) Swarm best (gbest)\n   iii) Inertia and acceleration coefficients\nd) Clip h values to [0,1] after updating and rescale to maintain sum(h) = n_points/2\ne) Track best solution found that satisfies all constraints\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\n- Start with n_points = 100 for better resolution\n- Use m = 50 particles to balance exploration and computation\n- Set inertia weight \u03c9=0.7, cognitive acceleration \u03c6_p=1.5, social acceleration \u03c6_g=1.5\n- Use initial_h_values if available, else use a random initialization with uniform distribution\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n- Each PSO iteration takes ~50ms with n_points=100\n- With budget_s=600, we can perform ~12,000 iterations\n- Include early termination if target C5 <= 0.3807 is achieved\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n- After optimization, validate that:\n   - sum(h) == n_points / 2 \u00b1 1e-6\n   - all h[i] in [0,1]\n   - computed C5 matches the evaluator output\n- Return best_h, best_c5, n_points in the required format",
